From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: recover after mismatched split RX indications

A mismatched continuation sets rx_confused, which rejects every subsequent
RX indication until the ring is reinitialized. Schedule recovery just as
the neighboring malformed-list and extraction error paths already do.
The caller only reschedules NAPI and cannot clear this condition itself.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt_rx.c
@@ -3311,6 +3311,7 @@
 		 || offload) {
 			ath10k_warn(ar, "split amsdu did not resume immediately\n");
 			htt->rx_confused = true;
+			ath10k_core_start_recovery(ar);
 			return -EIO;
 		}
 	}
